1
00:00:01,915 --> 00:00:06,479
Chapter 63. The crotch.

2
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:12,878
Out of the trunk the branches grow. Out of them the twigs. So in productive

3
00:00:12,879 --> 00:00:16,159
subjects grow the chapters.

4
00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:21,914
The crotch alluded to on a previous page deserves independent mention. It is a

5
00:00:21,915 --> 00:00:27,838
notched stick of a peculiar form, some 2 feet in length, which is perpendicularly

6
00:00:27,839 --> 00:00:32,878
inserted into the starboard gunnel near the bow, for the purpose of furnishing a

7
00:00:32,879 --> 00:00:38,238
rest for the wooden extremity of the harpoon, whose other naked barbed end

8
00:00:38,239 --> 00:00:40,958
slopingly projects from the prow.

9
00:00:40,959 --> 00:00:45,838
Thereby the weapon is instantly at hand to its hurler, who snatches it up as

10
00:00:45,839 --> 00:00:51,594
readily from its rest as a backwoodsman swings his rifle from the wall. It is

11
00:00:51,595 --> 00:00:56,799
customary to have two harpoons reposing in the crotch, respectively called the

12
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:59,518
first and second irons.

13
00:00:59,519 --> 00:01:05,359
But these two harpoons, each by its own cord, are both connected with the line.

14
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:10,878
The object being this, to dart them both, if possible, one instantly after

15
00:01:10,879 --> 00:01:16,719
the other, into the same whale, so that if in the coming drag one should draw

16
00:01:16,720 --> 00:01:19,914
out, the other may still retain a hold.

17
00:01:19,915 --> 00:01:25,039
It is a doubling of the chances. But it very often happens that owing to the

18
00:01:25,040 --> 00:01:30,079
instantaneous violent convulsive running of the whale upon receiving the first

19
00:01:30,080 --> 00:01:35,435
iron, it becomes impossible for the harpooner, however lightninglike in his

20
00:01:35,436 --> 00:01:41,359
movements to pitch the second iron into him. Nevertheless, as the second iron is

21
00:01:41,360 --> 00:01:46,318
already connected with the line, and the line is running, hence that weapon must

22
00:01:46,319 --> 00:01:52,479
at all events be anticipatingly tossed out of the boat. Somehow and somewhere

23
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:57,359
else the most terrible jeopardy would involve all hands tumbled into the

24
00:01:57,360 --> 00:02:00,159
water. It accordingly is in such cases.

25
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:05,914
The spare coils of box line mentioned in a preceding chapter making this feat in

26
00:02:05,915 --> 00:02:09,115
most instances prudently practicable.

27
00:02:09,116 --> 00:02:15,755
But this critical act is not always unattended with the saddest and most fatal casualties.

28
00:02:15,756 --> 00:02:20,799
Furthermore, you must know that when the second iron is thrown overboard, it

29
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:26,799
thenforth becomes a dangling sharpedged terror, skittishly curvetting about both

30
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:32,318
boat and whale, entangling the lines or cutting them, and making a prodigious

31
00:02:32,319 --> 00:02:37,838
sensation in all directions. Nor in general is it possible to secure it

32
00:02:37,839 --> 00:02:43,359
again until the whale is fairly captured and a corpse.

33
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:48,958
Consider now how it must be in the case of four boats, all engaging one

34
00:02:48,959 --> 00:02:54,799
unusually strong, active, and knowing whale, when, owing to these qualities in

35
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:58,958
him, as well as to the thousand concurring accidents of such an

36
00:02:58,959 --> 00:03:04,878
audacious enterprise, eight or 10 loose second irons may be simultaneously

37
00:03:04,879 --> 00:03:10,079
dangling about him. for of course each boat is supplied with several harpoons

38
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:14,878
to bend onto the line should the first one be ineffectually darted without

39
00:03:14,879 --> 00:03:20,079
recovery. All these particulars are faithfully narrated here as they will

40
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:25,838
not fail to elucidate several most important however intricate passages in

41
00:03:25,839 --> 00:03:30,360
scenes hereafter to be painted.
